     1                                  ; E1 Z22v (day2 round 2, base DET2): 32h-lattice detection. A zrl03/ah02 team (Chimera 32h line) writes its A's
     2                                  ; zombie entry (A load + 3Eh) to [0CC13h] at its instr 3; the bytes there are 31 FF (xor di,di) for zrl03/ah02 and
     3                                  ; E8 00 (call) for zchain3/4 (lattices 62h/52h). B reads [0CC13h] at instr 5 (before its own instr-6 write) and,
     4                                  ; if the word at that address is 0FF31h, sets its phoenix FAR_SEG immediate to 0FF8h = lattice 22h (10h below the
     5                                  ; 32h line) only when no V6-family team is present (V6 family keeps 42h). B + captured zombies use that immediate; A now reads the same
     6                                  ; FAR_SEG word from B's code through [4A17h] (= B's zombie_entry) in its phoenix_init, so A, B and all captured
     7                                  ; zombies always use one lattice. Turn cost: B +1 turn to phoenix_init (les ax pattern load and memory divisor
     8                                  ; pay for 2 of the 3 new instructions); A timing unchanged. Good_Test V6 is friend-provided (provenance below).
     9                                  ; D4 DET2: DET with B's [5D13h]/[0CC13h] writes back at instr 4/5 (rev1 rounds). DET's instr-3 [0CC13h]
    10                                  ; write tied with the zchain/zrl03/ah02 A write (instr 3) and lost the p0f13 hook half the time (screen n6sgd).
    11                                  ; D4 DET (day2, base rev1 KPHL): adaptive whole-team lattice. If a V6-family team is present (its B writes
    12                                  ; [4A17h] at instr 3; no other team in our fields writes that cell), every stream of ours (A, B, captured zombies)
    13                                  ; uses FAR_SEG 0FFAh = lattice 42h (10h below the V6-family 52h lattice, measured +0.28/+0.24 on leader2/3 cohorts
    14                                  ; in D4 W42 screen 0b3hc); otherwise FAR_SEG 0FFBh = 52h as in rev1 (W42's plain 2025/strong cost avoided).
    15                                  ; Detection: our B now writes [4A17h] late (instr 7), so at A's instr 5 and B's instr 5 the cell is still CCCCh
    16                                  ; unless a V6-family B wrote it at instr 3. A keeps the bit in BP; B patches the low byte of its own phoenix
    17                                  ; 'or dx,0FFBh' immediate (dec -> 0FAh) before any captured zombie can reach phoenix_init.
    18                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code (see the provenance comments below); DET edits by agent2 day2 role D4.
    19                                  ; COMBINE (night combination coordinator, 2026-10-04, base rev0): KPHL = KP + h34 (B099 KPH_B) + locpatA (B092 KL_A). A = KL_A unchanged; B = B099 KPH_B.
    20                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code; V6nohunt and all night edits by agent2 roles (see FINDINGS.md).
    21                                  ; B099 (wave 10, domain 9 R5-cost): KPH = B094 KP + B089 h34 (CX=0 zombie path mov bp,3400h -> 7000h, 1 byte).
    22                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided; V6nohunt by agent2; K by A031 (E1+SD+Z1 by A031/A022/A026); p0f13 by B064/B084; KP by B094; h34 by B089.
    23                                  ; B094 (wave 9, domain 4 R5-cost): KP = A031 K (E1+SD+Z1) + B084 p0f13 B edits ported onto K_B (Z1+SD).
    24                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided; V6nohunt by agent2; Z1 by A026, SD by A022, E1/K by A031; p0f by B064, p0f13 by B084.
    25                                  ; p0f13 edits: startup push cs/pop es -> mov [0CC13h],bx + les di,[si+es_ptr] (INT87 stays instr 12); both b/d searches
    26                                  ;   (startup and zom20a path) use window 0F EB F9 CC -> 0F FF 26 13 (patched tail = jmp [0CC13h]).
    27                                  ; Port note: in the zom20a path DX is now 0CCF9h after INT87, so Z1's int 86h there would write FF 1F F9 CC junk
    28                                  ;   over E1's A block (0FF80h..007Fh). It is replaced by mov dx,0CCCCh (same instruction count, no INT86 there);
    29                                  ;   E1's A block already covers 0FF80h..007Fh. The b/d (CX=0) path INT86 block is unchanged.
    30                                  bits 16
